<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<tt xml:lang="en-US"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml"
  xmlns:ttm="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#metadata"
  xmlns:tts="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#styling">
  <head>
    <metadata xmlns:ttm="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#metadata">
      <ttm:title>559342452 - 1_r4wabxtg - PID 1530551</ttm:title>
    </metadata>
    <styling>
      <style xml:id="basic" tts:textAlign="center" />
    </styling>
  </head>

  <body>
    <div style="basic">
        <p begin="00:00:06.840" end="00:00:17.780" tts:direction="ltr">Yeah. Doc, I</p>
        <p begin="00:00:17.780" end="00:00:19.260" tts:direction="ltr">keep missing deadlines,</p>
        <p begin="00:00:19.260" end="00:00:22.380" tts:direction="ltr">rent tuition, tailgate sign ups.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:22.380" end="00:00:24.340" tts:direction="ltr">Great Scott, Kelly.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:24.340" end="00:00:26.660" tts:direction="ltr">We time jump with EO month.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:26.660" end="00:00:29.580" tts:direction="ltr">It finds month ends in one line.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:29.580" end="00:00:33.260" tts:direction="ltr">That's great. But who is Scott?</p>
        <p begin="00:00:33.260" end="00:00:36.980" tts:direction="ltr">First, let's do a basic EO month</p>
        <p begin="00:00:36.980" end="00:00:40.660" tts:direction="ltr">to make sure the time portal is working.
<br />Watch closely.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:40.660" end="00:00:45.980" tts:direction="ltr">The EO month function has two arguments a
<br />date as well as an offset.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:45.980" end="00:00:50.340" tts:direction="ltr">The result is the last of the month based
<br />on the offset.</p>
        <p begin="00:00:51.140" end="00:00:55.860" tts:direction="ltr">For example, offset zero equal this month,</p>
        <p begin="00:00:55.860" end="00:00:58.700" tts:direction="ltr">negative one equal last month,</p>
        <p begin="00:00:58.700" end="00:01:00.420" tts:direction="ltr">plus one equal</p>
        <p begin="00:01:00.420" end="00:01:09.380" tts:direction="ltr">next month Kelly,</p>
        <p begin="00:01:09.380" end="00:01:11.380" tts:direction="ltr">go through the portal and bring back</p>
        <p begin="00:01:11.380" end="00:01:15.215" tts:direction="ltr">my plant that is on the desk. Let's do
<br />this.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:15.215" end="00:01:17.930" tts:direction="ltr">Grazing.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:24.010" end="00:01:27.290" tts:direction="ltr">Grazing. Wow, Doc.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:27.290" end="00:01:30.890" tts:direction="ltr">You did a good job watering the plan over
<br />the next few weeks.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:30.890" end="00:01:34.810" tts:direction="ltr">It looks great. Great Scott. It worked.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:34.810" end="00:01:38.570" tts:direction="ltr">It sure did. Who is Scott?</p>
        <p begin="00:01:40.500" end="00:01:43.940" tts:direction="ltr">I forgot to pay my credit card last month.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:43.940" end="00:01:47.260" tts:direction="ltr">Any chance I can go back to the last day
<br />of last month?</p>
        <p begin="00:01:47.260" end="00:01:49.540" tts:direction="ltr">You mentioned something about an offset.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:49.540" end="00:01:52.540" tts:direction="ltr">Kelly, you are absolutely right.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:52.540" end="00:01:58.260" tts:direction="ltr">We just need to adjust the offset to
<br />negative one to represent last month.</p>
        <p begin="00:01:58.260" end="00:02:02.900" tts:direction="ltr">Rewind one month, offset negative one.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:03.380" end="00:02:05.460" tts:direction="ltr">Right.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:08.660" end="00:02:11.500" tts:direction="ltr">No late fees. Yes.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:11.500" end="00:02:14.980" tts:direction="ltr">Great, Scott. It worked.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:18.200" end="00:02:22.600" tts:direction="ltr">Doc, is there any way I can jump ahead one
<br />month?</p>
        <p begin="00:02:22.600" end="00:02:25.920" tts:direction="ltr">I want to see how much I'll spend on my
<br />credit card this month.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:25.920" end="00:02:28.160" tts:direction="ltr">I'm starting to understand this stuff.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:28.160" end="00:02:30.920" tts:direction="ltr">Wouldn't it be offset plus one?</p>
        <p begin="00:02:30.920" end="00:02:34.640" tts:direction="ltr">Precisely. The offset would be plus one.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:34.640" end="00:02:38.000" tts:direction="ltr">In addition, we can use the get date
<br />function to</p>
        <p begin="00:02:38.000" end="00:02:41.400" tts:direction="ltr">represent today's date instead of hard
<br />wiring it.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:41.400" end="00:02:44.680" tts:direction="ltr">Get a date. I wish.</p>
        <p begin="00:02:57.930" end="00:03:02.890" tts:direction="ltr">I would never. You would never what,
<br />Kelly.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:02.890" end="00:03:05.770" tts:direction="ltr">Oh, nothing. It's nothing.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:08.330" end="00:03:11.450" tts:direction="ltr">Kelly, check this out.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:11.450" end="00:03:14.250" tts:direction="ltr">Did you know you can use the EO month</p>
        <p begin="00:03:14.250" end="00:03:18.410" tts:direction="ltr">to find the first day of the month? Watch
<br />this.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:19.470" end="00:03:21.550" tts:direction="ltr">Right.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:21.550" end="00:03:24.790" tts:direction="ltr">To get the first day of a month,</p>
        <p begin="00:03:24.790" end="00:03:31.950" tts:direction="ltr">land on the end of the previous month with
<br />EO month and add one day with D A.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:34.830" end="00:03:37.590" tts:direction="ltr">Doc, hold on.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:37.590" end="00:03:40.390" tts:direction="ltr">I just found the best deal on socks.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:40.390" end="00:03:45.150" tts:direction="ltr">Wow. 100 pairs of socks for $100.</p>
        <p begin="00:03:51.870" end="00:03:57.150" tts:direction="ltr">Before EO Month, we assembled it by hand.</p>
        <p begin="00:04:04.040" end="00:04:07.320" tts:direction="ltr">First day of this month,</p>
        <p begin="00:04:07.400" end="00:04:10.680" tts:direction="ltr">first day of next month.</p>
        <p begin="00:04:11.720" end="00:04:17.080" tts:direction="ltr">One day back to the last day of current
<br />month.</p>
        <p begin="00:04:17.080" end="00:04:19.720" tts:direction="ltr">Great Scott, Doc.</p>
        <p begin="00:04:19.720" end="00:04:22.360" tts:direction="ltr">That's not a query, that's a novel.</p>
        <p begin="00:04:22.360" end="00:04:25.040" tts:direction="ltr">The EO month is a great function to make</p>
        <p begin="00:04:25.040" end="00:04:28.280" tts:direction="ltr">finding the first and last day of a month
<br />easier.</p>
        <p begin="00:04:28.280" end="00:04:30.920" tts:direction="ltr">Who is Scott?</p>
    </div>
  </body>
</tt>
